<div type="mainBody">
<p> Please write and address <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">here</seg> kindest regards <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                    </p>
</div>
</div>

<div type="notes">
<note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ returned to Paris in mid-September 1922, seeking medical advice from his ophthalmologist Louis Borsch. Dissatisfied with his address at 9 rue de l’Université (see letter to Weaver of 20 September 1922, <hi rend="italic">LI</hi> 185-86), JJ rented a furnished flat at 26 avenue Charles Floquet for November (<hi rend="italic">JJ</hi> 537).</note>
